## Change rule

All material changes begin on a feature branch and enter `main` through a pull request. Direct production changes, hidden generated state, committed credentials, bypassed checks, and deployment from an unreviewed working tree are prohibited.

## Required pull-request evidence

Every PR states summary, risk, tests, documentation impact, and rollback. Security-critical paths named in `security/security-critical-paths.yml` require explicit security review. A material architecture, product, business, security, or UI decision updates canonical Markdoc and creates or amends an ADR.

## Required gates

- immutable dependency install with `npm ci`;
- incremental formatting and lint adoption;
- Astro type checking;
- unit tests;
- Markdoc source, link, and diagram validation;
- production build and built-link validation;
- secret, dependency, license, workflow, and vulnerability checks;
- browser smoke, accessibility, responsive, and reduced-motion checks when UI changes.

No gate may silently convert a blocking failure into success. An exception must be time-bounded, owned, mitigated, and recorded in `security/exception-register.yml`.

## Review and merge

AI output is a proposal, never approval. The accountable human reviews the actual diff and evidence. Because Beacon is currently a solo operation, the owner approval is not independent review; this limitation is recorded and must not be described otherwise.

## Release

Building, merging, staging, production approval, deployment, and verification are separate decisions. Production promotes the tested archive without rebuilding. Any missing digest, approval, credential, required check, or verification fails closed.
